# The engine's own log, written per run and keyed to nothing.
/.mule/infection.json

# The store itself is committed on purpose: a content-hash verdict is not
# machine-local state, so the next machine inherits the work instead of
# re-proving it. That is the whole point of .mule/verified.json — see
# docs/keying.md §4. It returns when there is a store to write.
